            <div xml:id="d379">

                <pb facs="0702" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./519:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-06T14:00:00-04:30">July 6, 1929—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>81. Department’s 23, June 13, 7 p.m. Foreign Office informs me that Minister of
                    Fomento states he has been unable to reach an agreement <pb facs="0703" n="567"
                        xml:id="pg567"/> with the representatives of Pan American Airways regarding
                    provisional permit but that he reiterated “sincere purpose of collaborating as
                    far as possible in the establishment of a fast and efficient mail service
                    between the two countries upon bases beneficial to both.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
